live browser console capture confirmed a pageerror ReferenceError: process is not defined at src/sdk/ServerHandlers.js:24:24 (client.isEditor = !process.env.EDITOR_TOKEN), thrown from within onClientConnect via WorkerEntry.js:141 -- the singleplayer in-Worker BrowserServer path (client/BrowserServer.js) calls the SAME onClientConnect as the real Node server, but process does not exist in a browser Worker context. The throw happens BEFORE MSG.WORLD_DEF/HANDSHAKE_ACK/SNAPSHOT ever send, so window.__terrain never gets set and the planet never renders -- confirmed via page.evaluate: hasWindowApp:true, hasTerrain:false, terrainCfg:null. This is a real pre-existing regression from the 2026-07-03 EDITOR_TOKEN auth-gate security commit (confirmed via git_log this repo's own commit, not a branch-merge/stale-code adoption issue -- the code on disk IS the intended latest version, it has a genuine cross-environment bug never tested against the Worker path). NOT caused by this session's optimization sweep or dependency bumps (git_log shows no touch to ServerHandlers.js in any of today's commits).